course: dictionary
lesson: 11714
title: A doctor's word: auscultate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to special jobs. Doctors and nurses use the word auscultate, which is a medical word. You may not know it, but the words around it give you clues. «The doctor placed the stethoscope on my back and asked me to breathe deeply while she auscultated my lungs.» A stethoscope, breathing and lungs all point to listening inside the body, so auscultate means to listen to sounds inside the body.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «listen to your chest». That is the plain-English version of auscultate. Auscultate is the doctor's word for the same idea, and it is a verb, so you can say a doctor auscultates a patient. The noun is auscultation: «The auscultation took only a minute.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The doctor listened to sounds inside my chest with a stethoscope» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. When a word is only used in one job, the clues in the sentence are often your best guide.
fact: Auscultate is a verb that means to listen to sounds inside the body.
fact: Doctors usually auscultate with a stethoscope, placed on the chest or back.
fact: The sounds they listen for include the heart and the lungs.
fact: The forms are auscultate, auscultates, auscultated and auscultating.
fact: The noun is auscultation, as in «The auscultation of my heart was quick and painless.»
exercise: «The doctor auscultated the patient's heart with a stethoscope.» What does auscultated mean? | Measured how tall the patient was | Looked at the patient's shoes | *Listened to sounds inside the patient's heart | Cut open the patient's skin
exercise: «The nurse used a stethoscope for the auscultation of my lungs.» What is auscultation? | *Listening to sounds inside the body | Cleaning a cut | Taking a photo of the body | Weighing a person on the scales
exercise: People say «listen to your chest». What is the doctor's word for this? | Inject | Diagnose | Bandage | *Auscultate
test: «Dr Patel auscultated the baby's lungs, and the sounds were clear.» What does auscultated mean? | *Listened to sounds inside the baby's lungs | Weighed the baby on the scales | Gave the baby a bath | Dressed the baby's wound
test: Which tool does a doctor usually use when they auscultate a patient? | *Stethoscope | Ruler | Thermometer | Bandage
exam: «When the doctor auscultates your chest, what is she doing?» | Taking your temperature | Measuring your height | Giving you medicine | *Listening to sounds inside your body
